nd is now 5. The comment above it and the tests both say five.\n- **`inventory.py`:** `recent(n)` returned one event too many (`[-n - 1:]`). It now returns the last `n`.\n- **`factory.py`:** `sample_books` was missing the `Emma` book, so I added `Book(\"Emma\", \"Austen\", 1815, 1)`. I made up the author, year and copy count, since the tests only check the title.\n\u001b[0m\nINFO  2026-10-22T19:27:16 +1ms service=session session=ses_e9aeb2bdaffeAdFVHojc2l6Vlf type=finish-step part\nINFO  2026-10-22T19:27:16 +1ms service=bus type=message.part.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-22T19:27:16 +0ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-22T19:27:16 +0ms service=session session=ses_e9aeb2bdaffeAdFVHojc2l6Vlf type=finish part\nINFO  2026-10-22T19:27:16 +1ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-22T19:27:16 +1ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-22T19:27:16 +1ms service=session session=ses_e9aeb2bdaffeAdFVHojc2l6Vlf sessionID=ses_e9aeb2bdaffeAdFVHojc2l6Vlf unlocking\n`python3 -m unittest` now passes: 16 tests, all OK. I didn't touch the tests. These are the fixes in `catalog/`:\n\n- **`books.py`:** `parse_book` now converts the year to an `int`.\n- **`search.py`:** it imported `normalize` from a module that doesn't exist. It now imports from `catalog.text`.\n- **`fees.py`:** `late_fee` added the daily fee to the number of days instead of multiplying. It now multiplies.\n- **`members.py`:** `MAX_BORROWED` was 3 and is now 5. The comment above it and the tests both say five.\n- **`inventory.py`:** `recent(n)` returned one event too many (`[-n - 1:]`). It now returns the last `n`.\n- **`factory.py`:** `sample_books` was missing the `Emma` book, so I added `Book(\"Emma\", \"Austen\", 1815, 1)`. I made up the author, year and copy count, since the tests only check the title.INFO  2026-10-22T19:27:16 +1ms service=bus type=session.idle publishing\n", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_request